{"book": "gate-da", "num": 18, "label": "18", "slug": "18-vector-spaces-quadratic-forms", "title": "Quadratic Forms", "tag": "Vector Spaces", "summary": "A quadratic form in $n$ variables $x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n$ is an expression of the type", "wordCount": 237, "readingTimeMin": 1, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "18.1", "title": "Definition and Basic Properties", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A <b>quadratic form</b> in $n$ variables $x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n$ is an expression of the type"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = \\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sum_{j=1}^{n} a_{ij} x_i x_j"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $a_{ij} = a_{ji}$, i.e., $A = [a_{ij}]$ is a symmetric matrix.\nEquivalently, in matrix notation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = x^T A x, \\quad x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ x_n\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad A = A^T."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Symmetric matrix representation:</b> Every quadratic form can be written uniquely using a symmetric matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = x^T \\frac{A + A^T}{2} x"}, {"t": "p", "x": "even if $A$ is not symmetric initially."}]}]}, {"id": "18.2", "title": "Diagonalization of Quadratic Forms", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $A$ is symmetric, there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P^T A P = D"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Then, by the change of variables $y = P^T x$, the quadratic form becomes"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = x^T A x = y^T D y = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\lambda_i y_i^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $\\lambda_i$ are the eigenvalues of $A$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "44", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Diagonalize the quadratic form"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x_1, x_2) = 4x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2 + x_2^2."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\text{eigenvalues } \\lambda_1 = 0, \\lambda_2 = 5"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{orthogonal matrix } P = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then $y = P^T x$ and $Q(x) = 0 \\cdot y_1^2 + 5 y_2^2 = 5 y_2^2$."}]}]}, {"id": "18.3", "title": "Positive Definite, Negative Definite, and Indefinite Forms", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let $Q(x) = x^T A x$."}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Positive definite: $Q(x) > 0$ for all $x \\neq 0$ ($\\lambda_i > 0$)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Positive semi-definite: $Q(x) \\ge 0$ ($\\lambda_i \\ge 0$)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Negative definite: $Q(x) < 0$ for all $x \\neq 0$ ($\\lambda_i < 0$)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Negative semi-definite: $Q(x) \\le 0$ ($\\lambda_i \\le 0$)"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Indefinite: $Q(x)$ takes both positive and negative values (some $\\lambda_i >0$, some $<0$)"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "45", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Determine the definiteness of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x_1, x_2) = 3x_1^2 + 2x_1 x_2 + x_2^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\text{eigenvalues } \\lambda_1 = 2, \\lambda_2 = 2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "All positive $\\implies$ $Q$ is positive definite."}]}]}, {"id": "18.4", "title": "Canonical Form Using Orthogonal Transformation", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "By applying an orthogonal transformation $y = P^T x$, a quadratic form can always be expressed in <b>canonical form</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = \\lambda_1 y_1^2 + \\lambda_2 y_2^2 + \\cdots + \\lambda_n y_n^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $y_i$ are new variables along orthogonal axes, and $\\lambda_i$ are eigenvalues of $A$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "46", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Bring"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x_1, x_2, x_3) = x_1^2 + 2x_1x_2 + 2x_1x_3 + 2x_2^2 + 2x_2x_3 + x_3^2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "to canonical form."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Compute $A$, find eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=0, \\lambda_2=1, \\lambda_3=5$, find orthogonal $P$, then $y=P^T x$, giving"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q(x) = y_2^2 + 5 y_3^2"}]}]}, {"id": "18.5", "title": "Geometric Interpretation", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The canonical form aligns the axes of the quadratic form with its principal directions. The signs of $\\lambda_i$ determine the shape of the surface:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Ellipsoid if all $\\lambda_i>0$"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Hyperboloid if eigenvalues have mixed signs"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Paraboloid if some $\\lambda_i=0$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "47", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Sketch the surface of $Q(x_1,x_2) = x_1^2 - x_2^2$."}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/va/fig010.png"], "caption": ""}]}]}, {"id": "18.6", "title": "Applications", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Quadratic forms are used to:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Test positive/negative definiteness of matrices"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Solve constrained optimization problems"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Analyze conic sections and 3D surfaces"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Diagonalize symmetric matrices (linking to orthogonal transformations)"}]}]}]}]}], "sectionCount": 6}